BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Once Upon a Time In Seattle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T180500
DTSTAMP:20261102T000000Z
UID:once-upon-time-seattle-2026-11-01-16:00:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:A perpetually living project\, Once Upon a Time in Seattle ret
 urns to Northwest Film Forum in a revised\, expanded (and shorter!?) edit 
 for this special encore engagement. Comprised of moments from 50 films sho
 t in Seattle (up from 47 in the previous iteration\,) and a few irresistib
 le facsimiles\, Once Upon a Time in Seattle is part love letter\, part loo
 ny action adventure\, and part free-associative meditation on the transien
 ce of landscape in a city that has always had a complicated relationship w
 ith honoring its past while moving swiftly (recklessly?) into the future.
 \n\nThere is no linear narrative\, and dialogue is kept to a minimum. The 
 city itself is both location and protagonist\, while the function of the h
 uman characters\, or perhaps more accurately\, ciphers\, is that of a vess
 el to move us through the city and occasionally offer loose context or com
 ic relief.\n\nNo single existing shot or sequence is sustained longer than
  a minute\, with most individual shots lasting less than 20 seconds\, and 
 over half clocking in at 5 seconds or less. The result is a deceptively co
 mplex amalgamation of wholly unrelated material\, and an impressively uniq
 ue editorial/directorial achievement.\n\nSurprisingly weaving numerous thr
 oughlines from the many disparate existing narratives\, while leaving much
  open to the viewer’s interpretation\, scene chronology floats between s
 eemingly non sequitur\, to quietly poignant\, depending on the viewer’s 
 own history with the city.\n\nA hyper-local\, one-of-a-kind film experienc
 e and an opportunity to examine Seattle’s ever-changing landscape as see
 n through the camera lens\, Once Upon a Time in Seattle offers a unique po
 rtal to examine our city’s topography (and vibe!) of the past\, both nea
 r and distant.\n\nIf you saw the premiere in September and loved it\, come
  see how it’s changed!\n\nCollide-O-Scope\, 2026\, United States\, 98 mi
 n\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/once-upon-time-seattle/\n
 \nEstimated start: 16:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
