BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Palestine Cinema Days 2026: Foragers (2022)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T202500
DTSTAMP:20261103T030000Z
UID:palestine-cinema-days-2026-foragers-2026-11-02-19:00:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:Foragers depicts the dramas around the practice of foraging fo
 r wild edible plants in Palestine with wry humor and a meditative pace. 
 Shot in the Golan Heights\, the Galilee and Jerusalem\, it employs fiction
 \, documentary and archival footage to portray the impact of Israeli natur
 e protection laws on these customs. The restrictions prohibit the collecti
 on of the artichoke-like ’akkoub and za’atar (thyme)\, and have re
 sulted in fines and trials for hundreds caught collecting these native pla
 nts. For Palestinians\, these laws constitute an ecological veil for legis
 lation that further disposses them from their land while the Occupation’
 s representatives insist on their scientific expertise and duty to protect
 . Following the plants from the wild to the kitchen\, from the chases betw
 een the foragers and the nature patrol\, to courtroom defenses\, Foragers 
 captures the joy and knowledge embodied in these traditions alongside thei
 r resilience to the prohibitive law. By reframing the terms and constraint
 s of preservation\, the film raises questions around the politics of extin
 ction\, namely who determines what is made extinct and what gets to live o
 n.\n\nJumana Manna\, Palestine\, 2022\, 65 min\, in Arabic with English su
 btitles\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/palestine-cinema-days-2026-forage
 rs/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SFCS at 10: Moonlight (2016)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261209T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261209T211500
DTSTAMP:20261210T030000Z
UID:sfcs-10-moonlight-2026-12-09-19:00:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:Special introduction by Timothy Hall of The People’s Critic
 \n\nA timeless story of human connection and self-discovery\, Moonlight ch
 ronicles the life of a young black man from childhood to adulthood as he s
 truggles to find his place in the world while growing up in a rough neighb
 orhood of Miami. At once a vital portrait of contemporary African-American
  life and an intensely personal and poetic meditation on identity\, family
 \, friendship\, and love\, Moonlight is a groundbreaking piece of cinema t
 hat reverberates with deep compassion and universal truths. Anchored by ex
 traordinary performances from a tremendous ensemble cast\, Barry Jenkins
 ’s staggering\, singular vision is profoundly moving in its portrayal of
  the moments\, people\, and unknowable forces that shape our lives and mak
 e us who we are.\n\nBarry Jenkins\, 2016\, United States\, 111 min\, in En
 glish\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/sfcs-10-moonlight/\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SFCS at 10: The Witch (2016)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T202500
DTSTAMP:20261120T023000Z
UID:sfcs-10-witch-2026-11-19-18:30:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:Special introduction by Bob Foster of Cinema Crazed\n\nNew Eng
 land\, 1630. Upon threat of banishment by the church\, an English farmer l
 eaves his colonial plantation\, relocating his wife and five children to a
  remote plot of land on the edge of an ominous forest—within which lurks
  an unknown evil. Strange and unsettling things begin to happen almost imm
 ediately—animals turn malevolent\, crops fail\, and one child disappears
  as another becomes seemingly possessed by an evil spirit. With suspicion 
 and paranoia mounting\, family members accuse teenage daughter Thomasin of
  witchcraft\, charges she adamantly denies. As circumstances grow more tre
 acherous\, each family member’s faith\, loyalty and love become tested i
 n shocking and unforgettable ways.\n\nIn this exquisitely made and terrify
 ing new horror film\, the age-old concepts of witchcraft\, black magic and
  possession are innovatively brought together to tell the intimate and riv
 eting story of one family’s frightful unraveling in the New England wild
 erness.\n\nRobert Eggers\, 2016\, United States\, 92 min\, in English\n\nh
 ttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/sfcs-10-witch/\n\nEstimated start: 18:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seattle Film Society Presents Locals Only: October 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T201000
DTSTAMP:20261030T020000Z
UID:seattle-film-society-presents-locals-only-october-2026-2026-10-29-19:0
 0:00-07:00
DESCRIPTION:POLAROID by Joey Greene: A young man is thrust into a terrifyi
 ng mystery when the Polaroid photos that he has taken reveal something tha
 t isn’t actually there. (3 Min)\n\nBEST FRIEND MATERIAL by Mel McCarthy 
 & Nathan Blanchard: A guys weekend goes wrong. (15 min)\n\nADHESION by Mar
 k Woo: A vain party clown suffocates in her own flesh-eating nightmare. (4
  min)\n\nMOTHER OF NIGHT by Mohamed Abdullahi & Rayana Mohamed: After a se
 ries of unexplained disappearances\, a night-shift waitress investigates a
  ghostly local myth and discovers the horror may be terrifyingly real. (13
  Min)\n\nLOOK AT THIS FREAK by Alex Furnas: A reunion of old friends is di
 srupted by a hated roommate and something else that’s even worse. (15 Mi
 n) \n\nThis event is presented in partnership with the Northwest Film Foru
 m. Join us for a screening and Q&A with drinks to follow at Linda’s Tave
 rn! See ya at the movies!\n\nOctober is for terror! On tap this month are 
 flesh eating nightmares and unexplained disappearances\, unnerving polaroi
 ds and weekends gone wrong. Not to mention a freak you won’t be able to 
 unsee. For all the horror-heads out there\, this one’s for you:\n\nhttps
 ://nwfilmforum.org/films/seattle-film-society-presents-locals-only-october
 -2026/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Parallax View (1974)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T210500
DTSTAMP:20261113T030000Z
UID:the-parallax-view-2026-11-12-19:00:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:After a presidential candidate is assassinated\, political rep
 orter Joe Frady begins to suspect that the mysterious Parallax Corporation
  may be involved. As he investigates\, others who share his suspicions sta
 rt turning up dead\, including his editor\, Bill Rintels. Eventually\, Fra
 dy uncovers a conspiracy bigger than anyone expected and must race to prev
 ent the corporation’s next big hit as this political thriller plays out 
 in an explosive game of cat and mouse.\n\nAlan J. Pakula\, United States\,
  1974\, 102 min\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/the-parallax
 -view/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tokyo Story (1953)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261128T181000
DTSTAMP:20261128T233000Z
UID:tokyo-story-2026-11-28-15:30:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:A profoundly stirring evocation of elemental humanity and univ
 ersal heartbreak\, Tokyo Story is the crowning achievement of the unparall
 eled Yasujiro Ozu. The film\, which follows an aging couple’s journey to
  visit their grown children in bustling postwar Tokyo\, surveys the rich a
 nd complex world of family life with the director’s customary delicacy a
 nd incisive perspective on social mores. Featuring lovely performances fro
 m Ozu regulars Chishu Ryu and Setsuko Hara\, Tokyo Story plumbs and deepen
 s the director’s recurring theme of generational conflict\, creating wha
 t is without question one of cinema’s mightiest masterpieces.\n\nYasujir
 ō Ozu\, Japan\, 1953\, 137 min\, in Japanese with English subtitles\n\nht
 tps://nwfilmforum.org/films/tokyo-story/\n\nEstimated start: 15:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
