BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You Sorta Know It's Gonna End
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T175500
DTSTAMP:20261116T003000Z
UID:you-sorta-know-its-gonna-end-2026-11-15-16:30:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:From staples of the independent Canadian scene\, filmmakers Ka
 lil Haddad and Ryan Steel present their new shorts cycle You Sorta Know It
 ’s Gonna End. Conceived as a video mixtape\, this hour-long compendium e
 choes the era of VHS rips\, featuring ten classic shorts from both directo
 rs\, alongside the new collaboration ‘BAND PRACTICE’.\n\nA bold new vo
 ice in queer experimental film\, Kalil Haddad’s global tour of his previ
 ous collection ‘He Never Dies : The Films of Kalil Haddad’ established
  him as a provocateur\; reckoning with a fraught visual aesthetic which in
 habits the burning edge of cultural danger and morality. He recently starr
 ed in Isiah Medina’s 2025 debut feature\, Gangsterism (2025).\n\nRyan St
 eel is a member of the Winnipeg Film Group\, previously working with estab
 lished voices of the Canadian avant-garde such as directors Guy Maddin (My
  Winnipeg\, Rumours) and Grace Glowiki (Dead Lover). He brings to this wor
 k his notion of material\, analog and DIY aesthetic – together\, craftin
 g You Sorta Know It’s Gonna End as a tangle of nostalgia\, masculine cri
 sis and caustic youth.\n\nKalil Haddad & Ryan Steel\, Canada\, 2025\, 62 m
 in\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/you-sorta-know-its-gonna-
 end/\n\nEstimated start: 16:50
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
